  "limitations": [
    "Reference lists are as resolved by Semantic Scholar's citation graph; S2 does not resolve every bibliography entry, so harvested counts are lower bounds on the true bibliographies. ragEvaluationSurvey2024 resolves to only 74 references, which is low for a survey and likely undercounts its bibliography.",
    "The 1,904 retrieved and 1,445 open-PDF stages have no released per-record list; recall is reported against the 1,399 deduplicated release, a lower bound on retrieval recall.",
    "Semantic Scholar year granularity is annual; papers dated 2026 cannot be split around the 2026-06-03 snapshot, so they are reported as a separate 'snapshot_year_ambiguous' bucket.",
    "The in-scope screen is title-only and deterministic; it neither reads abstracts nor resolves named systems, so it under-counts in-scope work (unfiltered recall is reported alongside).",
    "Frame stages are matched independently, not assumed nested: the 259 extracted full texts include a few foundational/core-reading papers (e.g. Lewis 2020 RAG, Self-RAG, CRAG) added outside the arXiv-retrieval dedup frame, so a reference can appear in the full texts without appearing in the 1,399 deduplicated release. 'Out of frame' therefore means absent from every released stage."
